# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ancre de version
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ne contient aucun code. Son unique fonction est de rendre impossible toute
# derive de version entre conteneurs : chaque role en depend a l'egalite
# stricte, donc apt refuse tout melange de trains de livraison.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Package: drumee-release
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Drumee release train anchor
 Declares the release train that every Drumee role package belongs to.
 This package ships no runtime code: it installs only
 /usr/share/drumee/release, a plain key/value file recording the release
 version, the APT channel it was published to, and the build timestamp.
 .
 Every drumee-role-* package depends on this exact version, which makes it
 impossible for two containers of the same deployment to run components
 from different releases.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exclusion mutuelle des roles
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chaque role fournit ET entre en conflit avec le paquet virtuel
# "drumee-role". Un paquet n'entrant jamais en conflit avec lui-meme, l'effet
# net est qu'un seul role peut etre installe a la fois : le monolithe ne peut
# pas etre reconstitue par accident dans une image.
#
# Si une variante tout-en-un devient necessaire un jour, elle prend la forme
# d'un paquet drumee-role-aio qui fournit le meme paquet virtuel et depend
# directement des composants.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Package: drumee-role-app
Architecture: all
Section: web
Provides: drumee-role
Conflicts: drumee-role
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         drumee-release (= ${binary:Version}),
         drumee-server-pod (= ${drumee:ServerVersion}),
         drumee-bootstrap (= ${drumee:BootstrapVersion}),
         drumee-node-runtime (= ${drumee:NodeRuntimeVersion}),
         nodejs (>= 22),
         nodejs (<< 23),
         mariadb-client,
         redis-tools
Description: Drumee application role (REST and push services)
 Runtime role for the container serving the Drumee backend: the REST API on
 port 24000 and the page/WebSocket server on port 23000, both supervised by
 pm2 in fork mode.
 .
 The pm2 supervisor and the pinned set of global Node modules are supplied
 by drumee-node-runtime rather than by an unpinned "npm install -g", so the
 JavaScript dependency set is versioned like everything else.

Package: drumee-role-web
Architecture: all
Section: httpd
Provides: drumee-role
Conflicts: drumee-role
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         drumee-release (= ${binary:Version}),
         drumee-ui-pod (= ${drumee:UiVersion}),
         drumee-static (= ${drumee:StaticVersion}),
         drumee-bootstrap (= ${drumee:BootstrapVersion}),
         nginx,
         libnginx-mod-stream
Description: Drumee web role (reverse proxy and static assets)
 Runtime role for the container terminating HTTP, serving the compiled LETC
 frontend bundles and the static asset tree, and proxying dynamic requests
 to the application role.
 .
 No build step happens here: drumee-ui-pod already contains the webpack
 output, produced once when the package was built in CI.

Package: drumee-role-media
Architecture: all
Section: video
Provides: drumee-role
Conflicts: drumee-role
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         drumee-release (= ${binary:Version}),
         drumee-bootstrap (= ${drumee:BootstrapVersion}),
         drumee-node-runtime (= ${drumee:NodeRuntimeVersion}),
         nodejs (>= 22),
         nodejs (<< 23),
         ffmpeg,
         graphicsmagick,
         libreoffice-core,
         libreoffice-writer,
         libreoffice-calc,
         libreoffice-impress,
         poppler-utils,
         dcraw,
         p7zip-full,
         fonts-liberation
Description: Drumee media role (document and media conversion)
 Runtime role for the conversion workers: video and audio transcoding,
 raster and RAW image handling, archive extraction, and office document
 rendering.
 .
 This role is deliberately isolated from the application role. It carries
 the heaviest dependencies in the whole platform, and it is the only
 component that parses untrusted user documents, so it runs with no
 database credentials and no inbound network exposure.
 .
 Only the LibreOffice modules actually used for conversion are pulled in,
 not the libreoffice metapackage.

Package: drumee-role-dns
Architecture: all
Section: net
Provides: drumee-role
Conflicts: drumee-role
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         drumee-release (= ${binary:Version}),
         drumee-bootstrap (= ${drumee:BootstrapVersion}),
         bind9,
         bind9-utils,
         bind9-dnsutils
Description: Drumee DNS role (authoritative zone server)
 Runtime role for the container answering as the authoritative name server
 for the deployment's zone, including the TSIG-signed dynamic updates used
 to answer ACME DNS-01 challenges for wildcard certificates.
 .
 Only required when the deployment answers challenges itself rather than
 through a provider API or a DNS-capable TLS terminator.

Package: drumee-role-mail
Architecture: all
Section: mail
Provides: drumee-role
Conflicts: drumee-role
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         drumee-release (= ${binary:Version}),
         drumee-bootstrap (= ${drumee:BootstrapVersion}),
         postfix,
         postfix-mysql,
         opendkim,
         opendkim-tools,
         spamass-milter
Description: Drumee mail role (SMTP and DKIM signing)
 Runtime role for outbound and inbound mail: notification delivery,
 invitation and onboarding messages, DKIM signing, and milter-based spam
 filtering.

Package: drumee-role-schemas
Architecture: all
Section: database
Provides: drumee-role
Conflicts: drumee-role
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         drumee-release (= ${binary:Version}),
         drumee-schemas (= ${drumee:SchemasVersion}),
         drumee-patch (= ${drumee:PatchVersion}),
         drumee-bootstrap (= ${drumee:BootstrapVersion}),
         drumee-node-runtime (= ${drumee:NodeRuntimeVersion}),
         nodejs (>= 22),
         nodejs (<< 23),
         mariadb-client,
         mariadb-backup
Description: Drumee schema role (database init and migration jobs)
 Runtime role for the run-once containers that create the yp/utils/template
 databases, seed the entity pool and system accounts, and apply pending
 schema patches before the application role is allowed to start.
 .
 The packages install migration payloads under /usr/share/drumee/patches
 only. Nothing touches the database at package configuration time, because
 no database exists during an image build. Application is driven by this
 role's entrypoint at deploy time and recorded in the schema_migrations
 table, which makes it idempotent and lets the application role refuse to
 start against an under-migrated database.

Package: drumee-role-infra
Architecture: all
Section: admin
Provides: drumee-role
Conflicts: drumee-role
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         drumee-release (= ${binary:Version}),
         drumee-infra (= ${drumee:InfraVersion}),
         drumee-bootstrap (= ${drumee:BootstrapVersion}),
         drumee-node-runtime (= ${drumee:NodeRuntimeVersion}),
         nodejs (>= 22),
         nodejs (<< 23)
Description: Drumee infrastructure role (configuration rendering job)
 Runtime role for the run-once container that renders the service
 configuration tree from the deployment's environment, writing it to the
 shared configuration volume consumed by the other roles.
 .
 Rendering happens in a chroot-style target directory, so this role never
 writes to a host path and never reconfigures the machine it runs on.
